Maintainer request 2026-10-16. Real case: dbio had .claude/skilletor.json from 2026-10-04 but enabled skilletor@getty only on 2026-10-16, so a fresh checkout had skills mentioning skilletor and none of the synced items. Wider: ~95 of the maintainer's repos enable @getty plugins (briefing, ruler) without declaring the getty marketplace in extraKnownMarketplaces (root cause: the getty-agent-team skill's settings template) — fine on his machine, unresolvable on anyone else's.

Goal: when sync runs for a project that uses skilletor (project skilletor.json / skilletor.local.json? decide — local is gitignored, so only the committed skilletor.json should trigger), skilletor makes sure the committed <project>/.claude/settings.json (1) enables skilletor@<marketplace skilletor is installed from> and (2) declares that marketplace in extraKnownMarketplaces; and (3) declares every other marketplace an enabledPlugins entry there references but the file does not declare (this fixes the briefing@getty gap in every skilletor project).

Constraints to design and record on the card:
- Source of truth for marketplace name and source: the user's Claude Code plugin state (~/.claude/plugins/known_marketplaces.json, installed_plugins.json; CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT when run as plugin). Never write a machine-specific source (a local directory/path source) into a committed file: skip it and say so in the report. claude-plugins-official needs no declaration.
- Only add, never remove or change existing keys; an explicit enabledPlugins["skilletor@x"] = false is the user's choice — leave it. Respect a settings.local.json? (it's per-machine; don't write there.)
- Keep the file's JSON valid and stable (key order kept, 2-space indent like Claude Code writes; no rewrite when nothing changes). A settings.json that does not parse: leave it, report.
- Opt-out config key (user and/or project file), named consistently with existing keys like gitignore; spec + README + bundled skill.
- Report line asks to commit .claude/settings.json once, like the .gitignore blocks.
- Codex: no equivalent known — state it.
- Tests: fresh project, existing settings with other keys, explicit false, path-sourced marketplace, unparseable file, idempotence, non-skilletor project untouched, user scope untouched.
Also: this repo's own .claude/settings.json enables briefing@getty and ruler@getty without the marketplace — it gets fixed by the feature (or by hand in the same change).

